# There was no .dockerignore at all until C8 / PR 57, so every build uploaded
# the whole working tree as context -- including .git, the two source tarballs
# (iw-src.tgz, plans.tgz), the local .env and, most of the point, scripts/ with
# the agent key in it.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs app/, alembic/, alembic.ini and requirements.txt, so
# none of that reached the image. Build CONTEXT is not the image, and that
# distinction is the whole reason this was easy to leave undone. But the context
# is uploaded to the builder, cached, and shipped to Railway, and one edited
# COPY line -- `COPY . .` in a hurry -- is all that stands between "not in the
# image" and "in the image, in a layer, forever". This file makes that mistake
# cost nothing.

# Secrets and local configuration. First, deliberately.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
scripts/.agent-key
scripts/.agent-key*
*.pem
*.key

# Version control and its history
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python build and cache artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Test and lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local databases and dumps
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sql.gz
*.dump

# Archives that have no business in a build context
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Operator material: runbooks, ship scripts, QA notes, plans. None of it runs
# in the container, and scripts/ is where the agent key lives.
scripts/
qa/
docs/
_to_delete/
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tests do not ship. The image runs the app; the gates run before the push.
tests/
